WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.670 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  reality-tv can go light on the reality  sometimes and presenting events as  authentic and unaltered while secretly  scripting and staging important scenes  is common here are a few events that  survivalists bear grylls didn't really  have to survive but it sure made for a  better story on screen the Sierra Nevada  mountain region is home to some of the  last truly wild horses in the United  States and wild mustangs have lived in  this area for centuries in a season one  episode of man vs. wild grills was shown  attempting to lasso some of the steeds  but it turned out that these Mustangs  might not have been so wild after all  the crew reportedly hired them from a  trekking station near their filming  location these were actually relatively  tame animals that were accustomed to  being around humans according to a  Sunday Times of London reports of course  that doesn't play as well to audiences  what makes for a more interesting scene  showing grills trying to sling a lasso  around a wild mustang poor admitting  that the crew essentially rented a few  horses that weren't actually running  wild the answer is obvious everyone  knows that an active volcano poses a  threat because of all the lava and there  are other dangers that can be present  like toxic gas in an episode of man vs.  wild in which Grylls explores the Mount  Kilauea volcano in Hawaii he's shown  working to avoid patches of molten lava  and clouds of so-called killer gas but a  safety adviser for the show told The  Sunday Times that while the gas should  be avoided in large quantities the drama  on the show was heightened using  off-camera smoke machines as for the  lava itself the crew used burning coals  to make the scene look more dangerous an  active volcano is scary enough they  probably didn't have to add all that in  man vs. wild grills is supposed to be on  his own in whatever inhospitable  environment he ended up in after all  it's called man vs. wild not grills and  his crew lending a helping hand vs. wild  but it's been revealed that grills has  been assisted by his crew on several  occasions without letting the audience  in on the truth even when he was not in  immediate danger  get inside both IVC guns after serving  as a consultant on the show survival  expert mark why nerds told the times if  you really believe everything happens  the way it's shown on TV you are being a  little bit naive for instance in one  episode that Weinert worked on grills  supposedly built a raft using only  natural materials that he found around  him like hibiscus twine palm leaves and  bamboo  however Weinert said that he personally  worked with a team of builders to put  the raft together and it was taken apart  so grills could be filmed putting it  together on camera in addition to mark  Winer its grills and his crew often  brought on other survival experts as  consultants on man vs. wild  there was nothing shady about that in  particular as long as they weren't doing  grills it's work for him but on at least  one occasion a consultant later revealed  that this was exactly what was going on  Nick rumens worked with grills on an  episode of man vs. wild in Western  Australia Grumman's told the herald-sun  that while he enjoyed his experience  working on the show and thought that  grills was a good person overall viewers  should know that the show was  predominantly scripted Grumman's also  explained that he was often responsible  for building grills as shelters and  finding him animals to eat in this  episode it was snakes admitting he was  disappointed by the final cut of the  episode rumens added whatever he does  isn't survival but it's definitely  entertaining Les Stroud is the host of  the show survivor Man which had a  similar premise to man vs. wild  but Stroud insists that his show was a  much more realistic picture of what it's  like to survive in the wild and man vs.  wild was basically a sham Stroud is not  a big fan of grills and he made this  very clear in a reddit AMA in 2013 he  stated that many of the survival skills  that grills had taught on the show would  actually not be very helpful for example  Stroud singled out an episode in which  Grylls was shown squeezing drinking  water from elephant dung something  Stroud claims would be impossible unless  the crew specifically soaked it with  water beforehand that is a fun moral of  the story man vs. wild shouldn't be seen  as a realistic documentary style show  it's entertainment above anything else  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

